### wrait-backend API — run each request individually (JetBrains HTTP Client / REST Client).
### Edit the variables below, then run requests with the gutter "Run" button.
### Flow: run "POST /api/register" to get a token, paste it into @deviceToken above,
### then run transcribe / cleanup / tag (they send X-Device-Token: {{deviceToken}}).

@baseUrl = https://wrait-backend-git-simplify-25102016-santiks-projects-0fd5708c.vercel.app/
@proxySecret = SECRET_WRAIT_VALUE
@deviceId = a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345678901234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef123456
@deviceId2 = a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345678901234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef123478
### Token for the quota endpoints: paste one here, or run POST /api/register and
### copy its "token" from the response into this value.
@deviceToken =eyJkaWQiOiJhMWIyYzNkNGU1ZjY3ODkwMTIzNDU2Nzg5MDEyMzQ1Njc4OTBhYmNkZWYxMjM0NTY3ODkwYWJjZGVmMTIzNDU2In0.-OjvqQVJj6pK5vVK6Po-hrdUiX7fQry28qGc_cm85NM

### GET /api/hello — health check (no auth)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/hello
Accept: application/json

### POST /api/register — Mode A: issues a token. Copy "token" from the response
### into @deviceToken at the top, then run the quota requests below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Proxy-Secret: {{proxySecret}}
X-Device-Id: {{deviceId}}

### POST /api/register — Mode B: present the stored token; returns quota, no new token, not rate-limited
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Proxy-Secret: {{proxySecret}}
X-Device-Id: {{deviceId}}
X-Device-Token: {{deviceToken}}

### POST /api/transcribe — needs {{deviceToken}} (multipart audio; file must exist at ./tests/audio.wav)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transcribe?language=en
X-Proxy-Secret: {{proxySecret}}
X-Device-Token: {{deviceToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="audio"; filename="audio.wav"
Content-Type: audio/wav

< ./tests/audio.wav
--WebAppBoundary--

### POST /api/cleanup — needs {{deviceToken}}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cleanup
Content-Type: application/json
X-Proxy-Secret: {{proxySecret}}
X-Device-Token: {{deviceToken}}

{
  "transcript": "um, like, you know, the meeting was, uh, really productive, right? basically we covered all the points",
  "language": "en"
}

### POST /api/tag — needs {{deviceToken}}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tag
Content-Type: application/json
X-Proxy-Secret: {{proxySecret}}
X-Device-Token: {{deviceToken}}

{
  "text": "Today I went for a long run in the park and felt great afterwards. The weather was perfect.",
  "tags": ["exercise", "nature", "mood", "work", "food", "travel"]
}

### Negative: POST /api/transcribe with NO token → expect 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transcribe?language=en
X-Proxy-Secret: {{proxySecret}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="audio"; filename="audio.wav"
Content-Type: audio/wav

< ./tests/audio.wav
--WebAppBoundary--

### Migration window: POST /api/transcribe with legacy X-Device-Id only (no token)
### → 403 when strict; 200 when the backend runs with REQUIRE_DEVICE_TOKEN=false
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transcribe?language=en
X-Proxy-Secret: {{proxySecret}}
X-Device-Id: {{deviceId}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="audio"; filename="audio.wav"
Content-Type: audio/wav

< ./tests/audio.wav
--WebAppBoundary--
